CRITERION 2 - Mutations show warnings immediately.  PASS
======================================================================
JSON-fallback path (worker's test), verified by running it:
$ go test -count=1 -v -run Overlap ./internal/handlers/accounts/...
  --- PASS: TestHandleCreate_OverlapWarningsSurfacedInPartial (0.00s)
Body asserts body["Warnings"] is a non-empty []interface{} and one element
contains "usaa-checking.csv" -- read at handlers_test.go:428-466.

I did not accept "immediate" on the strength of a present-warning test alone,
because a stale pre-save re-load would also show a warning that happened to be
true beforehand. I wrote two falsifying probes (in $SCRATCH/b2, outside the repo)
that go red if the re-load ran before the save was visible:
$ go test -count=1 -v -run 'TestProbe_' ./internal/handlers/accounts/...
  --- PASS: TestProbe_UpdateOutOfOverlapClearsWarning (0.01s)
      (starts overlapping; POST /accounts/a-wide narrows the pattern; asserts the
       swapped-in partial NO LONGER contains "Pattern overlap warning")
  --- PASS: TestProbe_DeleteClearsWarningOnPartial (0.01s)
      (starts overlapping; POST /accounts/b-narrow/delete confirm=yes; asserts the
       partial no longer contains the marker, and that the delete persisted)
Both pass, so the buildPageData re-load observes post-save state.

