CRITERION 7 - The SaveWithWarnings deviation.  CLAIM VERIFIED; BEHAVIOUR HOLDS
======================================================================
The worker's claim is factually correct:
$ grep -n "accounts\.Save\|accounts\.SaveWithWarnings\|accounts\.Mutate" internal/handlers/accounts/handlers.go
  190:  err := accounts.Mutate(...)     <- handleDelete
  265:  err = accounts.Mutate(...)      <- handleAddAnchor
  343:  err = accounts.Mutate(...)      <- handleDeleteAnchor
  478:  err = accounts.Mutate(...)      <- applyForm, used by handleCreate AND handleUpdate
  (529/533/536 are comment text only; NO call to accounts.Save or
   accounts.SaveWithWarnings appears anywhere in the file)
So "where it fits" fits nowhere: there is no Save call site to convert, and
switching Mutate to Save/SaveWithWarnings would surrender Mutate's atomic
load-modify-save. The deviation is justified.

I then verified the BEHAVIOUR criterion independently of the mechanism, on every
mutation handler, not just create. Reading the source, all five paths end with the
identical post-save pair `data, _ := buildPageData(r)` then `renderList(w, r, data)`:
  handleCreate       handlers.go:143-144
  handleUpdate       handlers.go:159-160
  handleDelete       handlers.go:206-207
  handleAddAnchor    handlers.go:303-304
  handleDeleteAnchor handlers.go:379-380
and buildPageData re-reads through accounts.Load(store) at handlers.go:541.

Source reading is not proof, so each path was exercised end-to-end in rendered
